diff --git a/backend/vendor/README.md b/backend/vendor/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..190b13c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/backend/vendor/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+Vendored from `lmxxf/dlss5-on-amd-9070xt-porting` at commit
+`7ef24e7c1498bce59738277e174249866608c4ed` (September 23, 2026).
+
+Source mapping:
+
+- `hip_reference_network.h`, `packed_weights.h`, `hip_device_properties.h`,
+  and `hip_api.h`: upstream `Development/HIP/`.
+- `LmxxfProductionOptions.h`: upstream `src/`.
+- `LICENSE.lmxxf`: upstream MIT license; HIP ABI declarations also retain AMD's
+  license notices inside their headers.
+
+Local modifications:
+
+- `hip_api.h` loads Linux `libamdhip64.so.7`, `.so.6`, or the unversioned soname
+  with `dlopen`/`dlsym`. `/opt/rocm/lib` and an explicit `DLSSLOP_HIP_LIBRARY`
+  path are supported. All network execution remains native HIP.
+- `hip_reference_network.h` rejects the Windows-only F8 hotkey option instead
+  of calling Win32 keyboard APIs. The scheduler and mathematical operations are
+  otherwise unchanged.
+- The worker clears the production option's block-skip set by default; its
+  `--performance` flag restores upstream's skipped blocks 42, 43 and 46.
+
+These host headers are ordinary C++17. Compiling the worker does not require a
+HIP SDK or linking to a particular HIP runtime. Actual inference requires the
+matching Linux GPU code objects, model weights, and a gfx1201-capable runtime.
+No model weights are vendored here.
